      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CORPSMAN (6) has the right mix of recent merit and grade relief. Her Scone sixth in a BM58 reads better than the bare result, with early and straight interference before she worked home to be beaten just under four lengths, and her Coonabarabran fourth in a BM66 also had merit after a slow start. TICKLE MY TOSEN (3) comes off a four-and-a-half-length Bowraville Class 1 win as favourite, though that was picnic company and this is harder. LA BELLA ROSA (5) was plain at Taree, yet the quick back-up, BM58-to-BM50 drop and return to a track-and-trip win keep her capable of running into it if she improves on that latest effort. CRASHMYPLAYA (2) has improvement to come and is worth keeping safe.",
